<div class="note"><b class="h">Local claim risks</b><ul class="chips"><li>Hail</li><li>Tornadoes</li><li>Heavy snow &amp; ice dams</li><li>Rock River flooding</li><li>Wind</li></ul><p class="housing"><b>Housing mix:</b> Historic homes in Haight Village and Churchill’s Grove, mid-century ranches, newer east-side subdivisions.</p></div>

<h2>Rockford homes</h2>
<p>Rockford’s older neighborhoods, including the Haight Village and Churchill’s Grove historic districts, hold Victorian, Italianate and Prairie-influenced homes with wood siding, plaster walls and detailed trim. The mid-century neighborhoods around them are full of brick and frame ranches, and the east side and Loves Park add newer subdivisions and commercial corridors along East State Street.</p>
<h2>Weather in the Rock River Valley</h2>
<p>Rockford sits far enough north to catch heavy snow and long freezes, which means ice dams and frozen pipes every winter. Spring and summer bring hail and tornadoes. On March 31, 2023, a tornado struck nearby Belvidere and collapsed part of the Apollo Theatre’s roof during a concert, a reminder of how fast severe weather develops here. The Rock River also floods low-lying areas in wet years.</p>
<h2>What Rockford owners dispute</h2>
<ul>
<li>Ice dam leaks where the carrier covers the ceiling but not the wet insulation and sheathing.</li>
<li>Older homes where matching wood siding and trim isn’t priced.</li>
<li>Hail claims on ranches with older, brittle shingles that can’t be repaired.</li>
<li>Commercial and industrial roofs on manufacturing buildings.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Serving the region</h2>
<p>We work in Rockford, Loves Park, Machesney Park, Belvidere, Cherry Valley and the surrounding Winnebago and Boone County communities.</p>

<h2>Services available in Rockford</h2>
<p>Every Illinois Insurance Appraiser service is available to property owners in Rockford and nearby communities, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/appraiser-services/named-appraiser-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/appraiser-services/illinois-homeowner-claim-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraiser-services/association-commercial-claim-appraisal/">Commercial, Condo &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraiser-services/hailstorm-roof-claim-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraiser-services/tornado-derecho-claim-appraisal/">Tornado, Derecho &amp; Wind Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraiser-services/basement-backup-water-claim-appraisal/">Basement, Backup &amp; Water Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraiser-services/fire-soot-smoke-claim-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from Rockford owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Are ice dams covered?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>The water damage they cause is often covered; removing the ice itself usually isn’t. Read your policy and document the damage promptly.</p></div></details><details><summary>My older home has plaster walls. Will the carrier pay for plaster?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Plaster repair is more expensive than drywall. If plaster is what was damaged, like kind and quality usually means pricing plaster or an equivalent repair.</p></div></details></div>
